      "title": "Missing absolute-path executable is not mapped to ErrUnavailable",
      "message": "exec.ErrNotFound is only returned when the executable is looked up on PATH by bare name. If the executable is an absolute or relative path that does not exist (for example a full path to powershell.exe), Start fails with an *fs.PathError wrapping fs.ErrNotExist. That does not match exec.ErrNotFound, so the missing helper is reported as a generic ProcessError instead of app.ErrUnavailable. Callers that fall back on ErrUnavailable will not do so in that case.",
      "suggestion": "Also match fs.ErrNotExist (import \"io/fs\"): `if errors.Is(err, exec.ErrNotFound) || errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) {`. Be aware that this can also match a missing file the helper itself reports, so check Start errors separately if that matters.",
